<!--
doc/src/sgml/ref/cypher_create.sgml
PostgreSQL documentation
-->

<refentry id="cypher-create">
 <indexterm zone="cypher-create">
  <primary>CYPHER CREATE</primary>
 </indexterm>

 <refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>CREATE</refentrytitle>
  <manvolnum>7</manvolnum>
  <refmiscinfo>SQL - Language Statements</refmiscinfo>
 </refmeta>

 <refnamediv>
  <refname>CREATE</refname>
  <refpurpose>create the cypher elements</refpurpose>
 </refnamediv>

 <refsynopsisdiv>
<synopsis>
CREATE <replaceable class="parameter">path_pattern</replaceable>
</synopsis>
 </refsynopsisdiv>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Description</title>
  <para>
   The <command>CREATE</command> clause is a clause that creates graph elements such as vertices and edges.
When you want to create a vertex, you need to write a vertex-related pattern in the CREATE clause. 
You may create each element separately, but you may also create a pattern you want
at a time by listing the path in the CREATE clause. Be careful when creating a path at once. 
If it is not used with the MATCH clause like the first query, it creates a new data
even if there is the same data as the corresponding pattern (i.e. duplicate data).
You can use the <command>CREATE</command> command both standalone statement and clause that working with of another clause.
  </para>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Parameters</title>
  <refsect2>
   <title><literal>path_pattern</literal></title>
   <para>
    Representation about the cypher path pattern that you want to create
    See <xref linkend="cypher-path"/> for more examples.
   </para>
  </refsect2>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Examples</title>
  <para>
   To create vertex:
<programlisting>
-- Create empty vertex
CREATE ( );

-- Assign vertex label "person"
CREATE (:person);

-- Assign property key "name", property value "Edward"
CREATE (:person {name: 'Edward'});

-- Assign property key "name", property value 20
CREATE (:person {name: 'Alice', age: 20});

-- Create two vertices and assign the variable name a and b
CREATE (a {name:'Alice'}), (b {name:a.name})
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   To create edge:
<programlisting>
-- Create two vertices with its edge which is named 'likes'
-- It also have direction, start from E to A.
MATCH (E:person {name: 'Edward'}), (A:person {name: 'Alice'})
CREATE (E)-[:likes]->(A);

-- Create edge with property key and value
MATCH (E:person {name: 'Edward'}), (A:person {name: 'Alice'})
CREATE (E)-[:likes {why: 'She is lovely'}]->(A);

-- Create edge. It has same start and end vertex id
MATCH (E:person {name: 'Edward'})
CREATE (E)-[:IS_PROUD_OF]->(E);
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   To create path:
<programlisting>
-- Create vertices and edge.
CREATE (E:person {name: 'Edward'})-[:likes]->(A:person {name: 'Alice'});

-- Only if MATCH clause found the person 'Edward', create 'Alice' and edge
MATCH (E:person {name: 'Edward'})
CREATE (E)-[:likes]->(A:person {name: 'Alice'});

-- Only if MATCH clause found the person 'Edward' and 'Alice', create the edge between them
MATCH (E:person {name: 'Edward'}), (A:person {name: 'Alice'})
CREATE (E)-[:likes]->(A);
</programlisting>
  </para>
 </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
  <title>See Also</title>
  <simplelist type="inline">
   <member><xref linkend="cypher-match"/></member>
  </simplelist>
 </refsect1>
</refentry>



